<title>USA: Marathon cuts US posted crude price 75 cts.</title>
<headline>Marathon cuts US posted crude price 75 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX-Marathon Group, said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $20.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $19.40 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $20.75 and Oklahoma sweet is $22.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1633</p>
</text>
